 * ~~[[Security] Path Traversal Risk in File Operations #2995](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/2995)~~ - Path Traversal Risk in File Operations (closed as duplicate of [[Security] Path validation bypasses in archive extraction, transcript, and memory manager #3277](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/3277)). * [[Security] WhatsApp accountId path traversal in resolveDefaultAuthDir #2692](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/2692) - WhatsApp accountId path traversal in resolveDefaultAuthDir. ### Other Security. * [[Security]: npm moltbot@latest still points to squatter's package - README instructs unsafe install #3275](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/3275) - npm moltbot@latest still points to squatter's package. * [[Security] Support running gateway as isolated system user instead of personal user #2341](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/2341) - Support running gateway as isolated system user. * [[Security] Add rate limiting to webhook endpoints #2149](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/2149) - Add rate limiting to webhook endpoints. * [[Security] Ship package-lock.json for dependency auditing #2147](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/2147) - Ship package-lock.json for dependency auditing. * [[Security] Command Injection in Shell Execution #2991](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/2991) - Command Injection. * [[Security] Unsafe eval() Usage in Browser Context #2992](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/2992) - Unsafe eval(). * [[Security] Path validation bypasses in archive extraction, transcript, and memory manager #3277](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/3277) - Path Traversal (multiple locations). * [[Security] Insecure Deserialization - JSON.parse Without Validation #2996](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/2996)-3002 - Input validation, logging, permissions. * [[Security] HTTP Server Without Mandatory HTTPS #2993](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/2993), [[Security] Weak Cryptography - SHA1 Usage #2994](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/2994), [[Security] Missing Explicit CORS Policy #2998](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/2998) - HTTPS, SHA1, CORS. The #2991-3002 batch was submitted on 2026-01-27 within a 1-minute window, suggesting an automated security scan or coordinated audit report. ## Issue actions.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"93709605602e57be\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99931216\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fe88081e322f3a74\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Remote skills node cache grows unbounded without cleanup · Issue #6760 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fe88081e322f3a74\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/6760\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2da6cc705e2b72ed\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... # [Bug]: Remote skills node cache grows unbounded without cleanup #6760. [[Bug]: Remote skills node cache grows unbounded without cleanup](#top)#6760. The `remoteNodes` Map in the skills-remote module caches node metadata when nodes connect but never removes entries when nodes disconnect, causing memory exhaustion in environments with frequent node churn. nodeId,{});// Added, never removed} export function recordRemoteNodeInfo(node{nodeId string;}){upsertNode(node);// Called when nodes connect}. **Entry point:** Node registration when remote skill nodes connect to the gateway. Connection requires authentication via `authorizeGatewayConnect()` or device token verification at `src/gateway/server/ws-connection/message-handler.ts:570-590`. * High (requires race condition, specific config, or timing). **Prerequisites:** Gateway must accept remote skill node connections. | Availability | High | Memory exhaustion from stale node entries |. 1. Run a gateway that accepts remote skill nodes. 4. Node records include `Set` of binary paths, increasing memory per entry. Modify `src/gateway/server/ws-connection.ts` to call a new cleanup function:. // In skills-remote.ts, add: export function removeRemoteNodeInfo(nodeId string) void void{remoteNodes.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2da6cc705e2b72ed\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99899167\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ef88c3fffb7ece93\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nopenclaw/openclaw\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ef88c3fffb7ece93\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues?q=roadmap+OR+%E8%A7%84%E5%88%92+OR+future+OR+plan&page=4\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7532faa7ab41fb9c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n#38283 · barnacle-openclaw opened on Mar 6, 2026. · pgondhi987  opened on Mar 31, 2026. · koen666  opened on Mar 31, 2026. * ### fix(gateway): harden control UI HTTP host header validation against DNS rebinding. channel: bluebubblesChannel integration: bluebubblesChannel integration: bluebubbles. channel: discordChannel integration: discordChannel integration: discord. channel: feishuChannel integration: feishuChannel integration: feishu. channel: googlechatChannel integration: googlechatChannel integration: googlechat. channel: imessageChannel integration: imessageChannel integration: imessage. channel: lineChannel integration: lineChannel integration: line. channel: matrixChannel integration: matrixChannel integration: matrix. channel: mattermostChannel integration: mattermostChannel integration: mattermost. channel: msteamsChannel integration: msteamsChannel integration: msteams. channel: nostrChannel integration: nostrChannel integration: nostr. channel: signalChannel integration: signalChannel integration: signal. channel: slackChannel integration: slackChannel integration: slack. channel: telegramChannel integration: telegramChannel inte